# PlayKiln conventions

- This repo is an **APK factory**, not a single product.
- New apps live under `apps/<date>-<slug>/` with unique `applicationId`
  `com.gexetr.<slug>`.
  - `com.gexetr` is the developer account's existing Play namespace; already
    published apps use it, so every new slot must match.
  - An applicationId is permanent after the first Play upload — never change it for
    a slot that has shipped.
  - The rule lives in `scripts/lib/namespaces.mjs`; import it, do not restate it.
- Stack: **Kotlin + Jetpack Compose + Material 3 + Gradle KTS**.
- The developer account's public contact address is **`v.sobolenko.vs@gmail.com`**. It is defined
  once in `scripts/store-kit.py` (`DEFAULT_CONTACT_EMAIL`) and is the default every new
  `store/listing.json` receives, so no slot ships the generator's `support@example.com`
  placeholder. It is a **public support address, not a secret** — Play publishes it on the listing,
  so it does not belong in `.env`; that rule governs credentials. A slot may override it, and a
  hand-authored value is never rewritten.
- A store pack must not carry a reserved-host placeholder into a listing. `scripts/store-kit.py`
  reports `contactEmail` / `privacyPolicyUrl` values on `example.com` (and `localhost`, and a
  non-HTTPS scheme) as unfinished in the generated human-checks list; the privacy policy URL has no
  default, because it has to be hosted somewhere the owner controls.
- Do **not** copy `.cursor/`, `.agents/`, or OpenSpec factory config into a slot.
- Do **not** use Flutter, React Native, Expo, or Next.js for new slots.
- Improve the root harness when the same mistake repeats across apps.
- Secrets/keystores never committed. Use `.env.example` placeholders only.
- Cursor and Codex are peers — see `harness/dual-agent.md`.
